# infra/ is TRACKED. It holds logic and shared names only. A filled-in
# environment file holds the identifiers for one deployment and must stay
# outside the repo, so ignore any .env here except the two that belong:
# config.env (names used in every environment) and the .example template.
infra/*.env
!infra/config.env
